      "message": "fix(post): Tormach programs end at the top of Z - no trailing G30\n\nThe Tormach mill post ended M9, M5, G53 G0 Z0, G30, M30. A bare G30\nmoves every axis to the stored G30 position, so in the user's PathPilot\nHub run (770MX sim, stored G30 at machine Z -1.5611) the end lifted to\nthe top of travel and then drove the tool back down below the part top.\nThe program now ends at the lift: M5, G53 G0 Z0 (or the machine's stated\nsafe Z, #495), the EndUnits word if any (#596), M30. No G0 A0 is added.\nThe G30 before each tool change is unchanged: retract() keeps it, the end\nuses the new liftZ() alone.\n\nThe 33 Tormach mill NC goldens lose their last G30 line and nothing else.\nPinned by tormach_program_end (every shipped Tormach mill, a stated safe\nZ, a 4th-axis job), with tormach_post / tormach_safe_retract /\ntormach_end_units updated to the new ending.\n\nFixes #1594\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
